# Depth-dependent rate and state parameters for the megathrust,
# converted from zab_TzT.dat by ab2profile.py.  That table gives a-b(z)
# from a subduction geotherm and laboratory a-b(T); here b is held
# constant at 0.0150 and a = b + (a-b).
#
# a-b spans -0.00350 to +0.02404 over 0.00 to 223.67 km depth.
# Velocity weakening between 4.03 and 55.45 km depth;
# most weakening a-b = -0.00350 at 5.53 km.
# The table began at 3.10 km; it is continued to 0.00 km at a-b
# = +0.00302 so the shallowest elements are not flat-extrapolated.
#
# Linear interpolation between control points; end values extend beyond.
# depth_km        a         b
